    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, but the analytical profile highlights **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) as our foundational cornerstones. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a exploitable matchup against V\u00e1squez (xERA 4.89), with a +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance; he draws Gibson, whose 5.87 xERA is the softest on the board, and the +16% park factor combined with his #2 spot in the order makes him a premium start. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.33) also warrants strong consideration, as his aggressive platoon advantage against Castillo (+14%) provides the necessary leverage to maintain efficiency despite facing a competent arm.\n\nThe decision-making process was most difficult regarding our bench spots, specifically the omission of **Nolan Schanuel** (44.14). While **Nolan Schanuel** technically cleared our 40.0 floor, he was edged out by the optimization of platoon-heavy roles and current order projections for players like **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Wade Meckler** (41.07); although he avoids the bench, his efficiency score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Griffin Jax (xERA 3.52) and the uncertainty of a pending lineup position. \n\nWe are closely monitoring the status of **Jacob Wilson** and **Wade Meckler**, both of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending\" status; any shift lower in the batting order would necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores. While **Nasim Nunez** (48.39) makes the lineup despite a lower raw score, we are factoring in his speed profile, as we prioritize stolen base potential to mitigate the risk of his #9 spot in the order. Owners should note that **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the IL, and we continue to bench **Miguel Vargas** and **Brayan Rocchio** today as their matchups against elite arms like Yamamoto and Skubal drag their projected output below our critical performance threshold.",
